{"name":"Daydream","hex":"#e3ebae","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"daydream","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spontaneous series of thoughts while awake not connected to immediate reality."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have such a series of thoughts; to woolgather."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/daydream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Daydream (Mariah Carey album)","blocks":[{"text":"Daydream is the fifth studio album by American singer-songwriter Mariah Carey. It was released on September 26, 1995, by Columbia Records. The follow-up to her internationally successful studio album Music Box (1993) and the holiday release Merry Christmas (1994), Daydream differed from her earlier works by incorporating stronger elements of urban music."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/95/Mariah_Carey_-_Daydream.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daydream_(Mariah_Carey_album)","wikidata":"Q835788"},{"title":"Daydream (The Lovin' Spoonful song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Daydream\" is a song by the Canadian-American folk-rock band the Lovin' Spoonful. Written by John Sebastian, it was issued as a single in February 1966 and was the title track of the band's second album, Daydream, released the following month. The song was the Spoonful's third consecutive single to enter the top ten in the United States, and it was their best performing to that point, reaching number two. The single's European release coincided with a British and Swedish promotional tour, leading the song to be the band's first major hit outside North America. It topped sales charts in Canada and Sweden, and it was ultimately the band's most successful record in the United Kingdom, where it reached number two."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Daydream_-_The_Lovin%27_Spoonful.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daydream_(The_Lovin'_Spoonful_song)","wikidata":"Q3019328"},{"title":"Daydreaming","blocks":[{"text":"Daydreaming is a stream of consciousness that detaches from current external tasks when one's attention becomes focused on a more personal and internal direction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Daydreaming_Gentleman.jpg/330px-Daydreaming_Gentleman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daydreaming","wikidata":"Q6028924"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Boys_II_Men.jpg/500px-Boys_II_Men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Boys_II_Men.jpg/1280px-Boys_II_Men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Boys_II_Men.jpg/500px-Boys_II_Men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boyz II Men in 1995, the same year they collaborated with Carey on \"One Sweet Day\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoys_II_Men.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Mariah_Carey_One_Sweet_Day_Madison_Square_1995.jpg/500px-Mariah_Carey_One_Sweet_Day_Madison_Square_1995.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Mariah_Carey_One_Sweet_Day_Madison_Square_1995.jpg/1280px-Mariah_Carey_One_Sweet_Day_Madison_Square_1995.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Mariah_Carey_One_Sweet_Day_Madison_Square_1995.jpg/500px-Mariah_Carey_One_Sweet_Day_Madison_Square_1995.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte